cff-version: 1.2.0
title: "BEAST: Bayesian Exascale Atmospheric Swin Transformer"
message: "If you use this software, please cite the paper given under preferred-citation."
type: software
license: MIT
version: 0.0.1
repository-code: "https://github.com/RAI-SCC/beast"
abstract: >-
  BEAST is a PyTorch library for probabilistic weather forecasting with
  Bayesian neural networks at scale. Its Bayesian Swin Transformer predicts
  global atmospheric states at 0.25 degree resolution and quantifies both
  aleatoric and epistemic uncertainty. A 4D parallelization scheme, which
  combines domain and tensor parallelism with uncertainty parallelism over the
  ensemble members, lets a single model span thousands of GPUs.
keywords:
  - atmospheric forecasting
  - uncertainty quantification
  - exascale computing
  - artificial intelligence
  - domain parallelism
  - sampling parallelism
